experiment.prespecified:
Fixed 2026-11-20, before any result of this definition was read (owner: "start experiments with the breeder
flags in the zoo, make a few arms"). classes-18 is the gate (RULES 16); small and medium (starts 1-360) follow
right after it: breeder cases are rare, and 18 starts show safety only.
kill-first is the owner's #556 rule with its companions: kill first (stoppable), never rest with breeders
known (rest), and walk out of a slow crowd that cannot be fought (crowd); all adds the exit and the avoidance.
Gate:
- no config_error; one binary; each arm's five values in borg.txt and in params-core.json of the death replays;
- every cell ends in death, turn_cap or borg_stopped; frozen-turn bursts classified and key outliers listed;
- death bundles reproduced;
- in ctl, none of the switches' notes: "# Breeders cannot be stopped", "# Fighting through the breeders",
  "# Leaving the breeders' room", "# Walking out of a slower crowd", and #644's "# Not resting: breeders to hunt."
Report per arm and per class, from every game's messages:
- deaths and causes, final and maximum level, deepest level; breeder deaths (the killer has MULTIPLY) and deaths
  to a slower or never-moving killer;
- paired rescued and newly killed against ctl (exact McNemar), and games identical to ctl;
- each switch's notes per game (the five above), and deaths within 500 game turns of one;
- breeder kills per game ("You have slain" a MULTIPLY race) and breeders created ("# Creating a monster" of a
  MULTIPLY race);
- breeder flees per game ("Fleeing (breeder level)", "Ignoring breeders (no recall)").
Context: borg-zoo#411 (stop and stop-avoid, 18 starts on ed8e270d): 1 / 3 / 2 deaths, none to breeders.
borg-zoo#448 (crowd, 360 starts on c3747cc9): 9 / 7 deaths, 2 rescued, 0 newly killed, 352 of 360 identical.
